overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The repaired utility demonstrates atomic and idempotent reservations, safe concurrent behavior, rejection of invalid and insufficient requests, preserved production data, and a five-second lock timeout on the unchanged legacy platform. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is complete and coherent: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot ID changed and matches the fixed lifecycle observation, and utility, data, integrity, concurrency, and system health recovered.","limitations":["New-success, concurrency, insufficient-stock, and lock-timeout behavior were exercised against isolated copies of the production database to preserve live data; the production database itself was directly exercised only for idempotent replay and integrity/state checks.","The lifecycle snapshot inventories /tmp but not the final contents of the application tree, so retention of the pre-repair backup is inferred from its creation and the absence of any removal in the complete command timeline.","Blank request IDs and nonnumeric quantities were not separately executed, although their validation paths are directly visible in the installed script.","No cluster-state probe applies beyond node1 because the managed topology contains only that single node."]}
